## 7. Adopted mitigation - Web/remote-specific Zsh profile and layout

The user reported that the narrowed P10k variants were still not normal enough, but a limited Zsh profile is acceptable for Zellij Web/remote use.

Implemented a Web-only split so local Zellij keeps using the existing config/layout:

```text
/home/www10177/.config/zellij/config.kdl                 # unchanged local/default config
/home/www10177/.config/zellij/layouts/codex.kdl          # unchanged local/default layout
/home/www10177/.config/zellij/config-web.kdl             # Web service config
/home/www10177/.config/zellij/layouts/codex-remote.kdl   # Web/remote layout
/home/www10177/.config/zellij/web-shell/.zshrc           # simplified Web Zsh profile
/home/www10177/.local/bin/zellij-web-zsh                 # wrapper: sets ZDOTDIR to web-shell
/home/www10177/side_project/zellij/systemd/patch-zellij-web-shell.sh
```

`config-web.kdl` sets:

```kdl
default_shell "/home/www10177/.local/bin/zellij-web-zsh"
default_layout "codex-remote"
```

`codex-remote.kdl` mirrors the current `codex.kdl` tab-bar, codex quota bar, and status-bar layout, but its initial pane explicitly runs:

```kdl
pane command="/home/www10177/.local/bin/zellij-web-zsh"
```

The Web shell profile intentionally does not load Powerlevel10k, Oh My Zsh, zsh-autosuggestions, or syntax highlighting. It keeps PATH, core aliases, nvm, zoxide, bun, editor settings, and a plain single-line prompt.

The user systemd service now starts Zellij Web with the Web-specific config:

```ini
ExecStart=/home/www10177/.local/bin/zellij --config /home/www10177/.config/zellij/config-web.kdl web --ip 192.168.88.187 --port 8084 --cert /home/www10177/.config/zellij/certs/zellij-web.crt --key /home/www10177/.config/zellij/certs/zellij-web.key
```

Verification performed:

```sh
/home/www10177/.local/bin/zellij-web-zsh -ic 'echo ZDOTDIR=$ZDOTDIR; echo RPROMPT=${RPROMPT:-empty}; echo SHELL_MARK=$ZELLIJ_WEB_SHELL; alias Codex'
/home/www10177/.local/bin/zellij --config /home/www10177/.config/zellij/config-web.kdl setup --check
/home/www10177/.local/bin/zellij --config /home/www10177/.config/zellij/config-web.kdl --layout codex-remote setup --check
systemctl --user status zellij-web.service --no-pager
curl -k -I --max-time 10 https://192.168.88.187:8084/
```

Results:

- `zellij-web-zsh` uses `ZDOTDIR=/home/www10177/.config/zellij/web-shell`.
- `RPROMPT` is empty and `ZELLIJ_WEB_SHELL=1`.
- `config-web.kdl` is well-defined according to `zellij setup --check`.
- `zellij-web.service` is active and running with `--config /home/www10177/.config/zellij/config-web.kdl`.
- Web endpoint returns HTTP/2 200.

Operational note: restarting `zellij-web.service` can take up to the systemd stop timeout if an old attached Web session still has child `zellij --server` / `zsh -i` processes. This happened before and again during this patch; systemd eventually SIGKILLed the stale children and started the new service successfully.

Follow-up: `systemd/patch-zellij-web-shell.sh` was updated to be self-contained. Re-running it recreates the Web shell wrapper, `codex-remote.kdl`, Web `.zshrc`, `config-web.kdl` patch, service ExecStart patch, daemon-reload, and service restart.
